## 1️⃣ Nature & Outdoor Adventures (≤ 15 mi)

| # | Attraction | Distance from the hotel* | What makes it special | Quick details |
|---|------------|--------------------------|-----------------------|----------------|
| 1 | **Delaware Water Gap National Recreation Area** | **≈ 9 mi** (≈ 15 min) | A spectacular river‑valley park that straddles the PA/NY border. Hiking, kayaking, and scenic drives abound. | • Main access points: **Portland** (PA) and **Milford** (NY). <br>• Popular hikes: **Mount Tammany** (moderate, 3 mi loop, great views) and **Dingmans Falls** (easy, 0.5 mi). <br>• No entrance fee; parking $5‑$10 at most trailheads. |
| 2 | **Bushkill Falls (Pennsylvania’s “Niagara”)** | **≈ 12 mi** (≈ 20 min) | A series of 8 waterfalls set in a lush, well‑maintained park. Perfect for families and photographers. | • Admission: $20‑$30 (adult), $12‑$18 (child). <br>• Open April – October (weather‑dependent). <br>• Bring sturdy shoes; some trails are steep and rocky. |
| 3 | **Lehigh Gorge State Park** | **≈ 13 mi** (≈ 22 min) | Rugged gorge carved by the Lehigh River, famous for world‑class white‑water rafting and mountain‑bike trails. | • Rafting runs (class II‑III) start at $70 per person. <br>• Bike‑trail hub: **D&L Trail** (12 mi paved, connects to the **Pocono** trail network). |
| 4 | **Camelback Mountain Resort** | **≈ 14 mi** (≈ 25 min) | Year‑round resort with a water‑park (Aquatopia), ski slopes, zip‑line canopy tours, and a mountain‑top restaurant. | • Winter ski lift tickets: $55‑$85 (adult). <br>• Summer water‑park day‑pass: $45 (adult). <br>• Family‑friendly; lockers and rentals on‑site. |

---

## 2️⃣ Family‑Friendly Attractions (15 – 30 mi)

| # | Attraction | Distance | Why it’s a hit | Practical info |
|---|------------|----------|----------------|-----------------|
| 5 | **Pocono Raceway** | **≈ 16 mi** (≈ 30 min) | One of the nation’s premier NASCAR tracks; hosts the **Pocono 400** and other motorsport events. | • Race‑day tickets start at $30 (general admission). <br>• Guided “Pit‑Crew Experience” tours (kids 5‑12) are $45 per child. |
| 6 | **The Crossings Premium Outlets** | **≈ 18 mi** (≈ 30 min) | A large outdoor shopping center with 100+ brand‑name stores (Nike, Coach, Michael Kors, etc.). | • Open 10 am‑9 pm (Mon‑Sat), 11 am‑7 pm (Sun). <br>• Free parking; no entry fee. |
| 7 | **Claws “N” Paws Family Fun Center** (Indoor arcade, mini‑golf, laser tag) | **≈ 19 mi** (≈ 30 min) | Great for a rainy‑day or evening activity with kids. | • Entry: $10‑$15 per person (includes 1 hour of play). <br>• Birthday‑party packages available. |
| 8 | **Pocono Environmental Education Center (PEEC)** | **≈ 20 mi** (≈ 35 min) | Interactive nature exhibits, live‑animal displays, and seasonal workshops for all ages. | • Admission: $8 (adult), $5 (child). <br>• Check the calendar for “Butterfly Release” events (May‑Sept). |

