## 3️⃣ Cultural & Historical Sites (30 – 45 mi)

| # | Attraction | Distance | What you’ll love | Details |
|---|------------|----------|------------------|---------|
| 9 | **Steamtown National Historic Site** (Scranton) | **≈ 35 mi** (≈ 45 min) | Restored steam locomotives, historic rail yards, and hands‑on exhibits about America’s rail heritage. | • Free admission; museum shop & guided tours $5‑$10. <br>• Open daily 9 am‑5 pm (except major holidays). |
|10| **Lackawanna Coal Mine Tour** (Scranton) | **≈ 36 mi** (≈ 45 min) | Descend 300 ft underground to see a preserved anthracite coal mine and learn about the region’s mining legacy. | • Tours run hourly, $15 per adult, $10 per child (5‑12). <br>• Closed on Mondays; wear sturdy shoes. |
|11| **The Shawnee Playhouse** (East Stroudsburg) | **≈ 38 mi** (≈ 50 min) | A community theater offering live productions, concerts, and film screenings in a historic 1930s building. | • Ticket prices $12‑$30. <br>• Check the schedule for family‑friendly shows (often on weekends). |
|12| **Delaware & Lehigh National Heritage Corridor** (various sites) | **≈ 40 mi** (≈ 55 min) | A scenic drive that links historic towns, covered bridges, and vineyards along the Delaware and Lehigh Rivers. | • Self‑guided driving tour; many stops are free. <br>• Great for a leisurely day‑trip with a picnic. |

